From b61f6b63ef4c9d1e7f88f4285310c679792ca7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:51:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(thread): pass control for thread milling -
 decreasing passes, finish and spring passes, depth allowance, M4 cutters

Internal and external thread milling gain ThreadPasses: a constant-chip-
area schedule (cumulative depth D x sqrt(i/n), the infeed the first
pass), a finishing pass of its own depth, spring passes on the final
radius, a radial depth allowance refused below zero and past a quarter
of the depth, and the spindle direction with the cutter's hand (climb
flips under M4; a cutter against its spindle is refused by name). Gated
at the operation door and in the kernel; flattened additive file / MCP
keys; Passes and Feeds page rows. M4 posts through a new MillSpindle
PARAM voiced by the Fanuc post and refused by name elsewhere. Defaults
keep every thread golden byte-identical; new golden
thread_mill_constant_area_spring_pass.cl.

Fixes #988

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
